{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"VERDICT ON THE (a)/(b) FORK: it is **(b)**, and the cause is a COLLATERAL REVERT. Change 2658's markers were CORRECT. The retraction was true when written and was invalidated four commits later. This ticket needs rescoping again.\n\n## The experiment\n\nWorktree at origin/main `9d5a7278c892`. Deleted exactly the two lines change 2658 added to `.github/mechanism-baseline.json`, changed nothing else:\n\n    $ python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check ; echo exit=$?\n    active=680 new=2 increased=0 stale=0\n      admitted  ci_gate::.github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml::Assert this tree is current with the tracked branch — bug eebc-6aa1-e45b-4325: ...\n      admitted  ci_gate::scripts/check_terraform_tree_currency.py — bug eebc-6aa1-e45b-4325:\n    exit=0\n\nBoth markers MATCHED. `--check` is green. So the markers were neither malformed nor mis-keyed — (a) is excluded as the cause.\n\n    $ pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -q\n    2 failed, 30 passed\n    FAILED test_check_passes_on_the_committed_tree - AssertionError: active=680 new=2 increased=0 stale=0\n    FAILED test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree - Extra items in the right set:\n      'ci_gate::.github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml::Assert this tree is current with the tracked branch'\n      'ci_gate::scripts/check_terraform_tree_currency.py'\n\nWith the two baseline lines restored (i.e. unmodified main): **32 passed**. So the two baseline lines were load-bearing and the marker alone does not satisfy the suite.\n\n## Why the retraction disagrees: the assertions it quoted were REVERTED\n\nThe retraction quoted `assert \"new=0\" in out or \"admitted\" in out` and `assert set(baseline) | admitted == live`. Neither exists on main. Current main, `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`:\n\n    line  94:  assert \"new=0\" in out and \"increased=0\" in out, out\n    line 358:  assert set(baseline) == live\n\n`git log -S'admitted' -- tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` returns exactly two commits:\n\n- **6125c5345f01** \"Pin review scanner contracts in Verified\" — ADDED the marker-honouring forms (it introduced two new `ci_gate` mechanisms, so it had to).\n- **9c7d78127696** \"Revert scanner-integration Verified gate\" — reverted 6125c534 WHOLESALE, for reasons entirely unrelated to the ratchet (vacuous Verified vote; the new required job was red on main and blocking Verified +1 for every open change). The revert took the marker-honouring assertions with it and restored the marker-blind forms.\n\nSo the retraction's \"PROOF ON CURRENT MAIN\" was accurate at the moment it was observed, and was undone by 9c7d78 along with the workflow. AC2's own note spotted that the workflow was reverted and called the proof stale — but inferred only that the *proof* was stale, not that the *assertions* had been reverted too. That is the missed step.\n\n**Net: on current main the ticket's ORIGINAL premise is true again.** A correctly-marked new mechanism passes `--check` and still fails two unit tests, and `--update-stale` refuses to write while anything is new. Change 2658's agent hit a real wall and had no sanctioned path; the hand-edit was the only route available. The AGENTS.md guidance and the tree genuinely disagree.\n\n## The (a) defect is real, but latent and NOT what bit 2658\n\nIndependently confirmed by construction — a well-formed marker whose key matches no detected mechanism is entirely silent:\n\n    >>> evaluate({\"lock::a.lock\":1}, {\"lock::a.lock\":1},\n    ...          {\"ci_gate::totally/wrong/key.py\":\"bug 1234 — justified\"})\n    exit: 0\n    active=1 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n\n`compare.py` `_partition` reads `markers.get(key, \"\")`, and `_blank_marker_errors` only reports markers whose reason is blank. A non-blank marker on an unmatched key is never mentioned on any line. So silent non-admission exists and is worth fixing — but it would NOT have helped 2658, whose markers matched.\n\n## Recommended rescoping\n\nTwo separable defects, and the current ACs describe only the second:\n\n1. **PRIMARY (the live one, currently unticketed):** the two assertions in `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` are marker-blind because a revert swept away their marker-honouring forms. Fix = re-apply what 6125c5345f01 had (`markers_for` still exists and is exported, so this is a re-application, not a design). Add a regression test that pins the tests themselves to honour markers, so the next wholesale revert of an unrelated change cannot silently re-open this. That last part is the real lesson: the ratchet's marker contract was only ever expressed inside a commit that was revertable for other reasons.\n2. **SECONDARY (this ticket's current ACs, still valid as written):** silent non-admission — a non-matching marker should name the key it was parsed as and the keys actually detected. Confirmed real above. Keep as-is, but it is a DX improvement, not the blocker.\n\nAC2 as written (\"reproduce 2601's marker and determine why it was not admitted\") should note that 2601 predates this analysis and that 2658 — the case with live evidence — was NOT a marker defect.\n\nI am NOT claiming this ticket: its ACs target (a), and an attestation against them would certify the wrong fix. Handing back for the rescoping decision. No code changed; scratch worktree only, main untouched.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788596371813353837,"uuid":"eb476a7d-fd3d-4878-8764-0f190d271e2f"}